'''Beli''' is a [[Torricelli languages|Torricelli language]] of [[Papua New Guinea]]. It is also known as ''Akuwagel, Makarim, Mukili''.

It is spoken in Mukili ({{coord|-3.685253|142.365984|type:city_region:PG|name=Mukili}}), Makapim ({{coord|-3.685606|142.383937|type:city_region:PG|name=Makapim}}), and other villages of [[Maimai Wanwan Rural LLG]] in [[Nuku District, Papua New Guinea|Nuku District]], [[Sandaun Province]].<ref name=e25/><ref name="UN-PNG">{{cite web |url=https://data.humdata.org/dataset/village-coordinates-lookup |title=Papua New Guinea Village Coordinates Lookup |author=United Nations in Papua New Guinea |work=Humanitarian Data Exchange |version=1.31.9 |date=2018}}</ref>

